{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Update UK National Speed Limits to 30-60-90mph",
        "additional_details": "We believe that, today, modern premium and standard cars feature high-grip compounds, advanced aerodynamics, and cutting-edge mechanical engineering that have reduced physical braking distances by more than half compared to the 1960s.\r\n \r\nWe feel it is time to trust driver judgment, acknowledge modern stopping capabilities, and align UK speed limits with 21st-century physics to reduce commuter stress, improve national productivity, and make logical progress.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to review and update the UK's national speed limits to a 30-60-90 framework: 30 mph in built-up urban throughways, 60 mph on A-roads, outside town, and 90 mph on motorways and dual carriageways to better reflect modern vehicle safety characteristics.",
        "closed_at": null,
        "closing_date": "2027-05-17",
